error[DATAMODEL001]: `datamodel:srcexpr` is not an attribute of the `datamodel` vocabulary
 --> tests/ui/datamodel001-misplaced-src.scx:1:165
  |
1 | ... datamodel="ecmascript" datamodel:srcexpr="'https://github.com/o/r/datamodels/json'" initial="a">
  |                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ unknown on `<scxml>`
  |
  = note: the `datamodel` vocabulary has exactly one attribute: `datamodel:src`, the URI of the data model's package
  = help: use `datamodel:src`, or remove the attribute

error[DATAMODEL001]: `datamodel:src` is not allowed on `<state>`
 --> tests/ui/datamodel001-misplaced-src.scx:2:17
  |
2 |   <state id="a" datamodel:src="https://github.com/o/r/datamodels/json">
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a `datamodel` attribute on an element that names no data model
  |
  = note: only `<scxml>` names a data model (SCXML 1.0 §3.2.1), so only `<scxml>` may name its package; an invoked document declares its own `datamodel` and `datamodel:src`
  = help: move the attribute to the `<scxml>` whose data model it names, or remove it
help: remove `datamodel:src`
